== Does the "myth" description need more subtlety? ==

In saying "{{xt|most mainstream Bible scholars consider Genesis to be primarily mythological rather than historical}}" does this require more subtlety?  Sure, Gen.1-11 is mythological, as discussed well in its "[[primeval history]]" article.  That's basically fine. But Gen.12-50 has very different genre characteristics; indeed the word "myth" never appears in the main body of its "[[patriarchal age|ancestral history]]" article.

So isn't the statement about the whole book "{{xt|...consider Genesis to be primarily mythological rather than historical}}" too blunt in not distinguishing the different genres across the primeval/ancestral divide?

Note: I'm basing this on the summary in the article lead.  But the myth-description in the main body (section "Genre") has the same over-generalisation problem, so it's probably better to start from there, then to reflect an appropriate summary back onto the lead.

